[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,6.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(7.8,0);
\foreach \y in {0,0.625,1.25,1.875,2.5,3.125,3.75,4.375,5.0} {\draw (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y);}
\foreach \y/\lbl in {0/0,1.25/50,2.5/100,3.75/150,5.0/200} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lbl$};}
\draw (0.8,0) rectangle (1.5,1.1);
\draw (1.9,0) rectangle (2.6,1.15);
\draw (3.0,0) rectangle (3.7,1.2);
\draw (4.1,0) rectangle (4.8,1.25);
\draw (5.2,0) rectangle (5.9,1.3);
\draw (6.3,0) rectangle (7.0,4.5);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {1.15/S1,2.25/S2,3.35/S3,4.45/S4,5.55/S5,6.65/S6} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {\lbl};}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-2.0,2.5) {Salary (\$ thousand)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3.9,-1.0) {Staff member};
\node[font=\small] at (3.9,6.1) {Staff salaries};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The column graph shows the yearly salaries of the six staff of a business, which are $\$44\,000$, $\$46\,000$, $\$48\,000$, $\$50\,000$, $\$52\,000$ and $\$180\,000$. Which measure of centre best represents a typical salary?
